attn-5 (docs/research/deepinfer/attention-kv.md, attn-5): Hadamard-rotated per-token-head KV, behind
VLLM_KV_HADAMARD=<head sizes> ("1" = 256; default unset = off, no code path changes).

Selected layers: decoder attention with an int8_per_token_head cache on TRITON_ATTN or CUSTOM (pthfa) and a
head size in the list (K and V the same size). int4_per_token_head is deliberately not selected: vLLM's int4
mode (v1/attention/ops/int4_per_token_head.py, reshape_and_cache_int4 / unified_attention_int4) already
rotates K, V and q by a randomized Hadamard (single_rht) and un-rotates the output. On Qwen3.8 with "1" that is the 16
full-attention layers of the target and the MTP layer (head size 256); the DFlash2 drafter's head-128 layers are
not selected. Such a layer builds the orthonormal Sylvester Hadamard H (D x D, entries +-1/16 at D = 256,
exact in bf16) at init on the model-init device, and then:
  - unified_kv_cache_update writes K H and V H (per token and head, before the per-token-head quantiser);
  - unified_attention_with_output runs the backend on q H into a scratch output and writes out_rot H to the
    caller's output (H H = I, so the result is P V).
q.k and P.V are unchanged in exact arithmetic; the per-token-head grid quantises flattened channels instead of
outlier channels (docs/research/deepinfer/cpu-checks/attn5_hadamard_kv.py measures the gain and the bf16 cost
of the three extra roundings). Both backends read K/V only from the cache, so the unrotated key/value passed
through to impl.forward are unused. The rotations live inside the two opaque custom ops, so the
torch.compile graph and cache key do not change; they are captured into CUDA graphs with the ops. Cost: four
[tokens x heads, D] x [D, D] matmuls per selected layer and step.

Test: bench/test_kv_hadamard.py (GPU: the layer's ops against the same calls without the knob; the cache really
holds rotated values). Applies on the stock image.

Apply: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz 0 -d /app/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < attn5-kv-hadamard.patch

--- a/model_executor/layers/attention/attention.py
+++ b/model_executor/layers/attention/attention.py
@@ -57,6 +57,57 @@ if TYPE_CHECKING:
 
 logger = init_logger(__name__)
 
+# attn-5 (research/deepinfer, docs/research/deepinfer/attention-kv.md attn-5):
+# VLLM_KV_HADAMARD=<head sizes> ("1" = 256; unset/"0" = off) rotates K and V of
+# every decoder layer with an int8_per_token_head cache on the TRITON_ATTN or
+# CUSTOM (pthfa) backend and one of those head sizes, per head, by the
+# orthonormal Sylvester Hadamard H (H = H^T, H H = I) before the cache write,
+# and the query by the same H before attention; the attention output (in the
+# rotated V frame) is rotated back. q.k and P.V are unchanged in exact
+# arithmetic; the per-token-head int8 grid sees flattened channels.
+# int4_per_token_head is not selected: vLLM's int4 mode already rotates by its
+# own randomized Hadamard (int4_per_token_head.py single_rht). Read once at
+# import; the rotations run inside the opaque
+# unified_kv_cache_update / unified_attention_with_output ops (eager or captured
+# with them), so the torch.compile graph and its cache key are unchanged.
+_KV_HADAMARD_DTYPES = ("int8_per_token_head",)
+_KV_HADAMARD_BACKENDS = ("TRITON_ATTN", "CUSTOM")
+
+
+def _kv_hadamard_head_sizes() -> frozenset[int]:
+    import os
+
+    raw = os.environ.get("VLLM_KV_HADAMARD", "").strip()
+    if raw in ("", "0"):
+        return frozenset()
+    if raw == "1":
+        return frozenset({256})
+    sizes = frozenset(int(x) for x in raw.split(",") if x.strip())
+    bad = [s for s in sizes if s < 2 or s & (s - 1)]
+    if bad:
+        raise ValueError(f"VLLM_KV_HADAMARD: head sizes must be powers of two, got {bad}")
+    return sizes
+
+
+_KV_HADAMARD_SIZES = _kv_hadamard_head_sizes()
+
+
+def _kv_hadamard_matrix(n: int, dtype: torch.dtype, device) -> torch.Tensor:
+    """The orthonormal n-point Sylvester Hadamard matrix (entries +-n^-1/2,
+    exact in bf16/fp16 for n a power of two up to 2^14)."""
+    h = torch.ones(1, 1, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)
+    while h.shape[0] < n:
+        h = torch.cat([torch.cat([h, h], 1), torch.cat([h, -h], 1)], 0)
+    return (h / n**0.5).to(dtype)
+
+
+def _kv_rotate(x: torch.Tensor, h: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+    """x [..., D] @ H in x's dtype (fp32 accumulate)."""
+    if h.dtype != x.dtype or h.device != x.device:
+        h = h.to(device=x.device, dtype=x.dtype)
+    return torch.matmul(x, h)
+
+
 
 def validate_kv_sharing_target(
     current_layer_name, target_layer_name, static_forward_context
@@ -453,6 +504,27 @@ class Attention(nn.Module, AttentionLayerBase):
         )
         self.backend = AttentionBackendEnum[self.attn_backend.get_name()]
         self.dtype = dtype
+        # attn-5: the layer's Hadamard (None = off); see _KV_HADAMARD_SIZES.
+        self._kv_hadamard: torch.Tensor | None = None
+        if (
+            head_size in _KV_HADAMARD_SIZES
+            and self.head_size_v == head_size
+            and kv_cache_dtype in _KV_HADAMARD_DTYPES
+            and attn_type == AttentionType.DECODER
+            and self.attn_backend.get_name() in _KV_HADAMARD_BACKENDS
+        ):
+            # Built on the model-init default device (the GPU), so no host
+            # copy ever happens inside a CUDA-graph capture.
+            self._kv_hadamard = _kv_hadamard_matrix(
+                head_size, dtype, torch.get_default_device()
+            )
+            logger.info_once(
+                "attn-5 VLLM_KV_HADAMARD: rotating K/V/Q of the %s layers with "
+                "head size %d (backend %s)",
+                kv_cache_dtype,
+                head_size,
+                self.attn_backend.get_name(),
+            )
 
         # For cuda-alike (CUDA and ROCM) and cpu platforms, we control how
         # torch.compile works by registering the attention as one giant
@@ -784,6 +856,10 @@ def unified_kv_cache_update(
         assert hasattr(attn_layer.impl, "do_kv_cache_update"), (
             f"{attn_layer.impl.__class__.__name__} does not support kv cache update"
         )
